From: Loïc Vigneron <loic@spin42.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: Disable L0s on the TI TUSB73x0

Behind the VENTUNO Q's PCIe switch, the TUSB7340 USB 3 controller's link
with L0s enabled logs about 45 receiver errors a second at the switch's
downstream port, and the root port escalates some of them to
uncorrectable errors, which ath11k and xhci cannot recover from. The
QCA2066 on the next port of the same switch, also with L0s, logs none,
and the errors stop with L0s off and L1 kept.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -2507,6 +2507,9 @@
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x10f4, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1508, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s);
 
+/* TI TUSB73x0 L0s exits produce a stream of receiver errors at its link partner. */
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_TI, 0x8241, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s);
+
 /* Realtek RTS525A generates a Replay Timer Timeout storm when L0s is enabled. */
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_REALTEK, 0x525a, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s);
 
